# Shopify theme push — code vs content

Merchant / Theme Editor data lives in JSON and must not be overwritten by routine deploys.

## Locked by `.shopifyignore`
- `templates/**/*.json`
- `config/settings_data.json`
- `sections/*-group.json`

## Default deploy (always)
```bash
npm run theme:push:code
# or equivalently:
npm run theme:push
```
Pushes only: `assets`, `sections/*.liquid`, `snippets`, `layout`, `locales`, `config/settings_schema.json`.
Use `--nodelete` (already in the script). Never run bare `shopify theme push`.

## Sync content down (safe)
After edits in Theme Editor:
```bash
npm run theme:pull:content -- --theme "ON DEV 2"
```

## Push content up (rare, explicit only)
Only when the user clearly asks to overwrite remote JSON / recover structure:
```bash
npm run theme:push:content -- --theme "ON DEV 2" --no-pull templates/page.about-us.json
```

## Never
- Push `page.about.json` / `page.about-us.json` / other template JSON unless the user explicitly requests content recovery
- Use `theme:push:all-unsafe` unless the user explicitly accepts wiping Theme Editor data
- Assume local JSON is newer than Theme Editor
